abstract = (u"\u2014Sovereign data protection legislation increasingly asserts extraterritorial jurisdiction over the global digital economy. Under Section 3(b) of India's Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act, 2023, data fiduciaries operating anywhere in the world must comply with statutory mandates when processing personal data of Indian data principals. In practice, global web platforms routinely deploy generic, boilerplate, or deceptive privacy policies that mask statutory non-compliance. General-purpose Large Language Models (LLMs) applied as auditors suffer from statutory hallucinations (58-88% error rates documented by Dahl et al.), cross-jurisdictional contamination (superimposing GDPR doctrines onto Indian law), and an epistemic failure to distinguish statutory silence from active breach. We present Ssense, the first domain-adapted Legal Small Language Model (Law-LM) and scalable inference architecture specifically fine-tuned and preference-aligned on India's DPDP Act, 2023 and DPDP Rules, 2025. Built upon Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, Ssense establishes a dual-track parameter-efficient architecture: a forensic statutory auditor (rank 128) and a citizen-facing legal dialogue model (rank 64), trained via rank-stabilized LoRA (rsLoRA) and Simple Preference Optimization (SimPO) over statutory reasoning traces, and released as Ssense-DPDP-7B, an open-weights legal model for the research community. We computationally model the DPDP Act by pruning 44 legislative sections into a 26-node actionable statutory decision tree with deterministic penalty weights. We introduce a three-step deductive reasoning chain and an omission firewall discarding findings derived from unstated practices, coupled with a deterministic Statutory Compliance Layer (SCL) as a lossless neuro-symbolic backstop (V_final = V_SLM union V_SCL). Our inference architecture integrates PagedAttention continuous batching, prompt KV cache pre-warming, speculative prompt lookup decoding (1.8x speedup), five-tier SHA-256 cache hierarchy, and XGrammar pushdown CFG decoding guaranteeing 100% schema validity. Empirical audits of ten real-world Indian fiduciaries (>500M MAU) yielded zero statutory hallucinations, zero false positives, and 18/18 certification axes cleared at 95% Wilson confidence lower bounds.")
